{
	"version": 5,
	"rows": [
		{
			"id": "e42WP-msGsBjn8ael",
			"description": "Dispersion Shield Field",
			"local_notes": "Shield 150 SP. Recharge: after 2 seconds without taking damage, regains 20 SP per second. Covers only attacks from the front and the shield-arm side, exactly as the Imperium Storm Shield's own field entry. Reflect: any single ranged hit that the field stops outright (does not exceed remaining SP) has a 1-in-6 chance (roll 1 on 1d) of being thrown back at its shooter at this weapon's own damage and armour divisor, resolved as an ordinary attack roll at the shield-bearer's own DX with no aiming penalty - the field's own kinetic energy lashing back rather than merely absorbing the blow.\n\nLore: The energy component of the Lychguard's paired dispersion shield: Codex: Necrons background and Black Library's Necron fiction both describe it not merely stopping incoming fire and blows but, now and again, hurling that force straight back at whoever struck it - a detail distinct enough from an ordinary Imperium force field that this project models it as an explicit, if infrequent, reflection rather than folding it silently into the shield's own recharge.\n\nDesign: Built on the exact regenerating-shield chassis in the Imperium's own fields.yaml, per framework.md's \"Personal force fields\" rules, with the Lychguard's own physical shield stats kept separately on the Dispersion Shield entry in Melee Weapons.yaml (the same split the Imperium Storm Shield uses). Pool and recharge are set above every Imperium field in this project (150 SP against the Storm Shield's own 160, at a matching 2-second/20-SP-per- second figure) since a Lychguard's shield is depicted stopping a comparable spread of fire to an Astartes storm shield without quite matching its absolute peak pool - appropriate for elite Necron bodyguard-class gear sitting alongside, not clearly above, the Imperium's own best personal fields. The reflect effect is new to this project's field family and is built as a simple 1-in-6 chance at the field's own already-defined damage and divisor (matching how this project's Volkite chain-on-kill and Tesla arc-on-hit effects reuse an existing attack profile rather than invent a new damage line) rather than a guaranteed counter-attack, keeping the shield genuinely a defensive item most of the time. Handling: weight 0 (folded into the shield item's own listed weight in Melee Weapons.yaml, the same convention the Imperium Storm Shield field entry uses).",
