			"quantity": 1
		},
		{
			"id": "el6uptB-2jGwh5x7t",
			"description": "Phase Shifter",
			"local_notes": "Shield 200 SP. Recharge: after 3 seconds without taking damage, regains 20 SP per second. Blocks ranged and melee attacks from any direction. Overflow phase: any single attack that would drain the field to 0 SP and still have damage left over does not carry that excess into the wearer's own necrodermis DR as an ordinary field overflow would; instead roll 1d - on a 5 or 6 the wearer's body phases fractionally out of reality for an instant and the excess damage is negated outright, on a 1-4 it applies normally against the wearer's DR. This is deliberately not literal invulnerability: an Overlord wearing a phase shifter can still die to a big enough hit, just less often than the fiction's own reputation for the item might suggest at first read.\n\nLore: Worn by senior Necron Overlords and Necron Lords, the phase shifter is consistently described across Codex: Necrons background, older Necron material and the RPG-line Necron- armoury write-ups as making its wearer extraordinarily hard to kill outright - \"near- invulnerable\" is the word background repeatedly reaches for, though even the fiction shows Overlords eventually brought down by sustained, overwhelming firepower rather than never dying at all.\n\nDesign: Built as this project's single strongest personal field, above even the Imperium's own Storm Shield (200 SP vs. 160, at a slower 3-second delay matching the Iron Halo/Storm Shield's own figure rather than the fastest fields' 2 seconds, since the anchor's own \"near- invulnerable\" framing calls for pool size over speed) plus the honest overflow-phase chance the assignment specifically calls for rather than a silently unbeatable field: a straight shield-points model alone would let any sufficiently patient, high-damage attacker eventually one-shot an Overlord through the field exactly like any other field in this project, understating \"near-invulnerable\"; a flat, unconditional negate would make the item unkillable and dishonest to the fiction's own occasional Overlord deaths. The 1-in-6-per- overflow compromise gives a real, if incomplete, second layer of protection precisely where the fiction's reputation and its own exceptions both point. Handling: 3 lb, a compact archeotech implant/regalia piece rather than a carried shield, befitting an item worn as much as equipped.",
			"tags": [
				"Force Field",
				"Energy Shield",
				"Xenos",
				"Necrons"
			],
