			"max_uses": 200,
			"quantity": 1
		},
		{
			"id": "egMh8b3CxtfHpcPml",
			"description": "Resurrection Orb",
			"local_notes": "Every ordinary Necron construct (not a named Overlord, Nemesor or other unique character) within 10 yards of the bearer adds +2 to its Reanimation Protocols HT roll (see the Necron ancestry's own Reanimation Protocols trait) rather than rolling at no bonus. Does not stack with the Rod of Covenant's own +1 (Melee Weapons.yaml); use the higher figure if both are somehow in range of the same unit.\n\nLore: Carried by a Necron Overlord or Cryptek overseeing a major engagement, the resurrection orb is described throughout Codex: Necrons background as strengthening the tactical link between nearby Necron warriors and their Tomb World's reanimation protocols, letting the fallen rise again more reliably than they would unsupported - a battlefield-command relic built specifically to make Reanimation Protocols itself work better, not a weapon or a shield.\n\nDesign: Modelled as a flat +2 bonus to the existing Reanimation Protocols HT roll (the mechanic framework.md's own Necrons section already defines for the ancestry) rather than as a new trait or mechanic in its own right, since the anchor's own instruction - \"boosts Reanimation Protocols of nearby Necrons\" - already names the exact roll this item should modify; inventing a parallel healing or resurrection mechanic here would duplicate work the ancestry trait already does. Set at +2 rather than a larger figure to keep it a real, noticeable edge without making Reanimation Protocols close to automatic for every unit near a command element, and explicitly excluded from stacking with the Rod of Covenant's own bonus so a fully-kitted Overlord's command retinue doesn't casually stack two of this project's own command items into a bonus neither alone was calibrated to represent. Handling: 5 lb, a carried relic-scale device rather than a weapon or armour piece.",
			"tags": [
				"Xenos",
				"Necrons"
			],
			"tech_level": "12^",
			"legality_class": "0",
			"base_value": "20000",
			"base_weight": "5 lb",
			"quantity": 1
		},
		{
			"id": "eCfm3lSzhcCNsIW3D",
			"description": "Phylactery",
			"local_notes": "The bearer may attempt a Reanimation Protocols HT roll even when no Tomb World, tomb complex or command relay is within range to ordinarily permit one (the GM's usual requirement for the roll to be attempted at all), and adds +1 to that roll when they do. Represents the phylactery's own small, self-contained consciousness-store standing in for the Tomb World's own reanimation network.\n\nLore: A small relic core, most associated in Codex: Necrons background and Black Library's Necron fiction with royal or particularly ancient Necrons (named Overlords, Nemesors and Phaerons feature it more than rank-and-file troops), that stores a fragment of its bearer's own consciousness independently of the Tomb World's central cryptek vaults - the specific reason certain Necron nobles can be cut off from their Tomb World for millennia, even destroyed outright, and still eventually rise again where an ordinary Warrior stranded the same way simply stays dead.\n\nDesign: Built directly from the anchor's own instruction (\"self-repair boost\") read against what actually distinguishes named Necron nobles from rank-and-file troops in the fiction: not a faster or larger single Reanimation Protocols roll (the Resurrection Orb above already covers \"better odds nearby\"), but the ability to attempt the roll at all far from any supporting infrastructure, which is the specific, repeatedly-told story beat this item exists to explain mechanically. The +1 on top is a modest personal echo of the Resurrection Orb's own group bonus, smaller because it applies to one bearer rather than a whole nearby formation. Handling: 2 lb, a small internal relic core rather than a carried or worn item in the usual sense - background typically describes it integrated into a noble's own necrodermis frame rather than equipped and removed like ordinary wargear.",
			"tags": [
				"Xenos",
				"Necrons"
			],
			"tech_level": "12^",
			"legality_class": "0",
			"base_value": "30000",
			"base_weight": "2 lb",
			"quantity": 1
		},
		{
			"id": "eGVBB8U0E8SYVuSGr",
			"description": "Sempiternal Weave",
			"local_notes": "Stacks with the wearer's own necrodermis natural DR (see the Necron ancestry's physiology traits) rather than replacing it - a Necron is never issued body armour in the usual sense, since its body already is its armour, so this entry adds to that baseline instead of covering it the way the Imperium's flak or carapace items do for an otherwise-unarmoured human.\n\nLore: A layer of living, self-repairing necrodermis threads worn over a Necron noble's existing metal body, referenced in Codex: Necrons background and older Necron material as an extra measure of protection reserved for Overlords, Crypteks and other high-value Necrons whose loss would matter more than a rank-and-file Warrior's - background is consistent that it thickens and reinforces the wearer's own frame rather than being a separate suit of plate bolted over it.\n\nDesign: Framework.md's own anchor: \"Sempiternal weave | Extra natural DR.\" Modelled as a flat +20 DR added on top of whatever the wearer's own ancestry-trait necrodermis DR already provides (Warrior 50 up to Overlord 100, per framework.md's Necrons table) rather than a stand-alone armour item with its own DR figure, since the anchor is explicit that this is additional protection layered onto an existing body, not a replacement suit - the same \"adds to, doesn't cover\" logic the assignment itself calls for. +20 is set as a genuinely meaningful bump (comparable to the jump from one Necron rank's own DR table entry to the next) without being large enough to make a woven cloak alone outclass simply being a tougher-bodied Necron in the first place. Handling: 8 lb, a worn layer rather than rigid plate - light next to any Imperium body armour in this project's own files, since it supplements an already-metal body rather than protecting soft tissue from nothing.",
			"tags": [
				"Xenos",
				"Necrons"
			],
			"tech_level": "12^",
			"legality_class": "0",
			"base_value": "16000",
